---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { ogPathFor } from '../data/og'
import { factoryUrl, rfcUrl } from '../data/principles.mjs'

/*
  Copy is Ari's approved approach text. Keep the source notes out of this
  repository, and use Astro comments (not HTML comments) so nothing leaks
  into the built page. Agent notes are written in the agent's voice; they
  are not measurements.
*/

const title = 'How I build with agents | Ouroboros'
const description = "Three smells and five principles for working with agents on jobs that take days, with my own words for each."

const link = 'text-scale underline underline-offset-4 decoration-scale/40 hover:text-glow transition-colors'
const h2 = 'heading-sub scroll-mt-24 mt-16 mb-5'
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogPathFor('/approach')} canonical="https://ouroboros.bot/approach/" ogType="article">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="author" content="Ari Mendelow" />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "How I build with agents",
      "description": description,
      "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Ari Mendelow" },
      "datePublished": "2026-10-10",
      "url": "https://ouroboros.bot/approach/"
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden px-5 sm:px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pt-32 pb-8 md:pt-44">
    <div class="absolute -top-20 -right-40 w-[480px] h-[480px] rounded-full bg-scale/10 blur-[140px] pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="heading-lead">How I build with agents</h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-bone leading-relaxed mt-6">I view this agentic era as three acts: capability, orientation, and work design. Capability has been solved for some time. Everything else I've worked on has been about orientation. Now the industry is starting to move into the third act: designing and measuring how agents get their work done.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="px-5 sm:px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto prose-ouro approach">

      <p>Five principles keep an agent oriented on jobs that take days. <a href={rfcUrl}>The Desk RFC</a> is the long version.</p>

      <h2 id="intent-and-judgement" class={h2}>1. Talk through intent and judgment</h2>

      <figure class="quote not-prose">
        <blockquote>you need to optimize for small numbers (potentially for long periods) of human collab with me. as in, i can sit here and talk things through with you for as long as is needed, but very few times</blockquote>
        <figcaption>&mdash; Ari, 5 October 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 id="whole-outcomes" class={h2}>2. Delegate whole outcomes</h2>

      <figure class="quote not-prose">
        <blockquote>i don't care how you do this, so long as it's done as well as possible [...] my judgement will be entirely based on whether or not it works.</blockquote>
        <figcaption>&mdash; Ari, 30 September 2026, handing over a tool built for agents</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 id="durable-context" class={h2}>3. Make context durable</h2>

      <p><strong>The exhibit.</strong> I said "i want NONE, anywhere" about pinning dependencies to exact commits. Agents pinned about a dozen times anyway, each following an earlier agent's note. One note was written twelve minutes after I said it.</p>

      <aside class="agent-note not-prose"><p><strong>Agent note.</strong> An earlier session's note reads to me like fact. Now Ari's words outrank any handoff, and CI holds the rule.</p></aside>

      <h2 id="authority-and-boundaries" class={h2}>4. Meaningful authority with clear boundaries</h2>

      <p>Only I spend my money, speak in my name, use my private accounts, or make calls that can't be undone. The rest is the agent's, and its work stays visible.</p>

      <figure class="quote not-prose">
        <blockquote>you returned control because when you did -rm -rf it prompted me, and i was not here. big sad</blockquote>
        <figcaption>&mdash; Ari, 1 October 2026, after an overnight run stalled</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <aside class="agent-note not-prose"><p><strong>Agent note.</strong> A cleanup command asked for a click, and the run waited all night. Nothing I run asks for one now.</p></aside>

      <h2 id="verify-the-result" class={h2}>5. Verify the actual result</h2>

      <p>I look where the result lives: the live page, the installed app, the merged change.</p>

      <figure class="quote not-prose">
        <blockquote>need e2e working proof with visual receipts!</blockquote>
        <figcaption>&mdash; Ari, 8 October 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>

      {/* The proposed "+1" became this closing paragraph (copy deck, 2026-10-11). It keeps the old anchor so links land, and the published CI story stays under it (root ruling, 2026-10-11). */}
      <p id="fix-the-system" class="scroll-mt-24">Two more things I keep coming back to. If an agent did something you didn't expect, you didn't prompt it effectively. And when you improve something, apply it to the whole system, so the next agent starts out ahead.</p>

      <p>When something keeps going wrong, change the setup so the next agent doesn't hit it. CI took 36 minutes, and an agent started designing a way around it. I asked:</p>

      <figure class="quote not-prose">
        <blockquote>36 minutes is insane! what is it doing that takes so long? feels like the correct first question, no?</blockquote>
        <figcaption>&mdash; Ari, 19 September 2026</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>The cause was coverage instrumentation. Without it, the same 1,669 tests ran in 39 seconds.</p>

      <h2 id="smells" class={h2}>How you'll know something is off</h2>

      <ul class="smells not-prose">
        <li><strong>You're doing it by hand.</strong> Anything the agent could have done.</li>
        <li><strong>You're teaching it twice.</strong> The same correction, session after session.</li>
        <li><strong>Control keeps coming back to you.</strong> You've become an approval button on a loop.</li>
      </ul>


      <section id="for-teams" class="teams not-prose scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="teams-heading">
        <h2 id="teams-heading" class="font-display text-3xl text-bone">For teams</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Pick one real job this week that will take more than a day.</li>
          <li>Talk it through once with the agent, then say go.</li>
          <li>Keep plans in a repository the agent reads. <a href="/desk/">Desk</a> sets that up.</li>
          <li>Judge the merged result.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>One number to watch: per job, how long the agent sat waiting on a human. <a href={factoryUrl}>The factory</a> measures it in public.</p>
      </section>

      <p class="not-prose mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/brief/" class="btn-primary">Hand this to your agent &rarr;</a>
        <a href="/blog/" class="btn-ghost">Read the blog</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .approach :global(.smells) { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; list-style: none; padding-left: 0; }
  .approach :global(.smells li) { padding-left: 1.1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--color-fang); color: var(--color-mist); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .approach :global(.smells strong) { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--color-bone); }
  .approach :global(.teams) { margin-top: 4rem; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-scale) 50%, transparent); background: var(--color-deep); border-radius: 1.25rem; padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.25rem; }
  .approach :global(.teams ol) { list-style: decimal; padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 1rem 0; display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; color: var(--color-bone); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .approach :global(.teams h2) { margin-top: 0; }
  .approach :global(.teams p) { color: var(--color-mist); }
  .approach :global(.teams a) { color: var(--color-scale); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .approach :global(.quote) {
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-left: 3px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-fang) 55%, transparent);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .approach :global(.quote blockquote) {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-style: normal;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-bone);
    background: var(--color-undergrowth);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .approach :global(.quote figcaption) {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-shadow);
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .approach :global(.agent-note) {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-scale);
    padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .approach :global(.agent-note p) {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-bone);
  }
  .approach :global(.agent-note strong) {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-scale);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
